New blog post: DB Design — The Three Normal Forms

Most database design guides explain normalization like a textbook. I wanted to try something different.

In this post, I show you flawed tables first — and challenge you to spot what's wrong before I reveal the answer.

Here's what it covers:
→ 1NF, 2NF, 3NF — each one introduced through a broken table and a "what goes wrong when..." question
→ The subtle difference between 2NF and 3NF (they look the same until you don't)
→ A four-step decomposition framework for splitting any messy table into clean, perpendicular pieces — no intuition required

My favourite line from the post:

"A column in 3NF depends on the key, the whole key, and nothing but the key — so help me Codd."

If you've ever stared at a table that felt "off" but couldn't articulate why, this framework will give you the vocabulary and the method.

🔗 https://roobystudio.com/posts/db-three-normal-forms/

#DatabaseDesign #SQL #BackendDevelopment #SoftwareEngineering #Normalization

